{"benchmark": "ifeval", "task_id": "1021", "sample_idx": 34, "model_name": "mistralai/mistral-small-4-119b-2603", "content": "PARAGRAPH 1\nTHIS STATEMENT PRESENTS A PROBLEMATIC VIEW OF LEGAL OBLIGATIONS BY IMPLYING THAT INDIVIDUALS HAVE THE AUTHORITY TO DETERMINE WHICH LAWS ARE BINDING BASED ON PERSONAL JUDGMENT. IT OVERSIMPLIFIES THE COMPLEXITY OF LEGAL SYSTEMS WHERE LAWS OFTEN SERVE AS ESSENTIAL MECHANISMS FOR MAINTAINING ORDER, PROTECTING RIGHTS, AND ENSURING SOCIAL COHESION. BY SUGGESTING THAT ONE CAN DISREGARD LAWS THEY DEEM \"BAD,\" THE STATEMENT UNDERESTIMATES THE POTENTIAL CONSEQUENCES OF SUCH ACTIONS, SUCH AS CHAOS, INJUSTICE, OR THE EROSION OF PUBLIC TRUST IN INSTITUTIONS. FURTHERMORE, IT NEGLECTS THE FACT THAT MANY LAWS ARE THE RESULT OF DEMOCRATIC PROCESSES INTENDED TO REFLECT THE WILL OF THE PEOPLE.\n\nPARAGRAPH 2\nTHE STATEMENT ALSO LACKS PRECISION IN ITS DEFINITION OF WHAT CONSTITUTES A \"BAD\" LAW, WHICH COULD LEAD TO SUBJECTIVE AND ARBITRARY APPLICATION. WITHOUT CLEAR CRITERIA, THIS FRAMEWORK COULD BE USED TO JUSTIFY NONCOMPLIANCE WITH LAWS THAT ARE INCONVENIENT OR UNPOPULAR RATHER THAN TRULY UNJUST. ADDITIONALLY, IT IGNORES THE LEGAL AND ETHICAL CONSEQUENCES OF DISOBEYING LAWS, INCLUDING POTENTIAL PENALTIES OR HARM TO OTHERS WHO MAY BE AFFECTED BY SUCH ACTIONS. INSTEAD OF ENCOURAGING RESPONSIBLE CITIZENSHIP, THIS STATEMENT RISKS PROMOTING A CULTURE OF ENTITLEMENT WHERE INDIVIDUALS PRIORITIZE THEIR OWN MORAL CONVICTIONS OVER THE COLLECTIVE GOOD.", "logprobs": [{"token": "PAR", "logprob": -0.2812701463699341}, {"token": "AG", "logprob": -5.722029527532868e-06}, {"token": "RAP", "logprob": -5.221230458118953e-05}, {"token": "H", "logprob": -9.298280929215252e-06}, {"token": " ", "logprob": -0.09002820402383804}, {"token": "1", "logprob": -6.83045873302035e-05}, {"token": "\n", "logprob": -0.10739771276712418}, {"token": "TH", "logprob": -0.38469022512435913}, {"token": "IS", "logprob": -0.0005098473629914224}, {"token": " STATE", "logprob": -0.9758018